--- S systematics ---
S1 LOS->3D: the law's statement is about the *line-of-sight* dispersion
   (sigma_los^2 = v_flat^2/2 in the isothermal reading, G03G/L49); the
   comparison is LOS-to-LOS by construction.  The alternative 3D reading
   (sigma_3D = sqrt(3) sigma_los) would raise every sigma_pred by +0.239
   dex: median |log10| would become 0.437 -> V1 FAILS under the 3D
   reading.  The data select the 1-D LOS reading.
S2 anisotropy: for constant beta in [-1, +0.5] the LOS dispersion of a
   cored isothermal sphere differs from the isotropic value by <= ~15%
   (<= +-0.06 dex envelope on pred/obs); the median is the robust statistic.
S3 binaries (Simon 2019 S2.1, verbatim): classical-dSph sigma robust
   (Olszewski+95 ... Spencer+17); UFD sigma mostly robust (Boo I: <3%;
   Segue 1: consistent after binary correction).  Known biased cases:
   Boo II and Tri II (bright binary, 5 and 6-13 stars) -- already carried
   as caveated/upper-limit rows.  One-way inflation bound ~20% (0.08 dex)
   on low-sigma UFDs; median impact <= ~0.03 dex.
S4 IMF: (M/L)_V = 1.5 adopted (Kroupa, stated).  Chabrier 1.2 -> log10 M*
   -0.10; Kroupa-upper 2.0 -> +0.12; Salpeter 3.0 -> +0.30; sigma_pred
   moves by 0.25 x that (<= 0.03-0.08 dex) -- verdicts are convention-
   robust:
   (M/L)_V = 1.2:  median |log10| = 0.244
   (M/L)_V = 1.5:  median |log10| = 0.222
   (M/L)_V = 2.0:  median |log10| = 0.195
   (M/L)_V = 3.0:  median |log10| = 0.162
S4 gas: 53/54 objects are gas-free (HI limits ~100-1000 Msun, S5);
   Leo T is the only gas-bearing object: if M_HI ~ M_* there, sigma_pred
   rises by 2^(1/4)-1 ~ +0.075 dex, still inside its 1-sigma band.

